      "why": "Best power/accuracy lever for this spec: it still yields 1 result/cycle so throughput = Fmax and the 50 MSPS floor is essentially free in sky130, while the register-every-m-stages schedule lets the search trade Fmax (which we have plenty of headroom in) for far fewer flip-flops, which is exactly where the min power_index objective lives. m is given the full 2..8 range so the search can find the minimum-register point that still clears 50 MSPS."
    },
    {
      "budget_share": 0.3,
      "family": "pipelined",
      "ranges": [
        {
          "choices": [ "trunc", "round" ],
