        },
        {
          "choices": null,
          "high": 3,
          "low": 0,
          "param": "frac_guard"
        }
      ],
      "why": "Safe reference family: one register per micro-rotation gives a very short critical path, so 50 MSPS is met with large margin, and it defines the fully-registered anchor of the area/power vs accuracy curve. Included so the front is not under-covered if the m>1 variants lose too much Fmax or do not actually save power."
    },
    {
